# Organization and Payroll: concrete native UI candidate

Base `0f812243c4af461bfd3685f8413ded84456f282b`. Owner proposed: `/root/integration_tests` for two new SSR module files only, after independent review and lane admission. Root owns shared lib.rs/style/test hookup; Company owner retains native_account.*. No implementation has started. Lenses: Essentialism, Systems Thinking, Red Team, Operability, Blast-radius and Zero-trust.

## Visual decisions against the actual prototypes

The three inspected1600×1000 screenshots show: Organization's broad canvas and nested cards; Payroll's period header, horizontal process, work area and evidence rail; Approval's compact decision inspector beside the inbox, with linked evidence, participants, reason and consequence together. Preserve that information hierarchy. Adapt the broad org chart into a vertical semantic hierarchy below960px; do not make320px users pan a diagram. Preserve evidence beside the subject on wide screens and immediately below it on narrow screens. Communications remains a separately navigable workspace destination; it is never substituted for a business inspector.

Use the parent's shared light theme: white surfaces on a quiet warm-gray workspace, thin neutral borders, restrained amber attention and green only for confirmed states, dark primary text, Korean-readable14–16px body type, compact20–24px heading, tabular numbers. Page max width1280px,24px gutters desktop/16px mobile,24px main gap,8px corner radius. Two-column task layout minmax(0,1fr)320px at ≥1100px; one column below. No fixed-height page content, text truncation of evidence/reasons, chart-only relation meaning, hover-only actions, or color-only state.

Reference decisions: adopt hierarchy cards, period/step context and nearby evidence; adapt auto-transfer step to statement/instruction/reconciliation; reject fixed headcounts/totals/sample deadlines, permission from rank, simulated progress, deleted approval history and buttons that do not invoke a real owner.

## Exact first implementation at the existing renderer boundary

Existing callable: `render_screens(&ShippingScreens, UiScreen::{Organization,Payroll})`. Existing authorized shape remains intact; no new backend, alternate app, preview binary, fixture path or universal screen generator. The seven proposed tests compile against today's names/types. They assert missing behavior, not the existence of new functions.

### Organization module (`src/organization.rs`)

`pub(crate) fn body(companies: ScreenSection<CompanyView>, units: ScreenSection<OrgUnitView>) -> impl IntoView` replaces the current organization body through a root-owned two-line call. All output remains SSR, with no script/island.

1. Root supplies the single page-level h1 (focused route “조직”, Home “내 업무”); module uses section headings only. Short current-view description and no invented Group name/effective date. Company cards form a separate “법인” region using actual legal_name/org_id/reg_no/version. OrgUnitView has **no Company FK**; it cannot honestly nest units under company cards or derive affiliation from names.
2. “조직 구조” is an ordered hierarchy list with explicit parent labels (avoid thousands of nested DOM levels for pathological chains), with each unit's actual name, readable revision, existing exact data-* keys and existing object record link. Parent-child identity comes only from parent_id matching another supplied unit. Source order is not hierarchy: parent must precede descendants even when input is shuffled.
3. Every supplied unit is retained once. Duplicate identities appear as an explicit “중복 식별자 확인 필요” conflict preserving both supplied labels and without an ambiguous object link; do not silently pick a winner. Missing/disclosed-excluded parents, self-links and cycles appear in a separate “상위 조직 확인 필요” group. Do not create/link a hidden parent or silently relabel a cycle as normal roots. Use a bounded traversal with a visited set, iterative stack and deterministic sibling order; no recursive stack overflow for deep chains, no repeated whole-vector scans. Handle duplicate IDs explicitly as a projection conflict before claiming a clean hierarchy.
4. The right context card “조직 변경 시 확인할 사항” explains the actual task: current/proposed parent, effective date, affected employments and approvals must be checked together; current displayed version remains visible. It is labeled guidance, never a fabricated pending change. Native `<details>` can disclose this guidance; do not show edit/date/submit controls until owner-bound state/actions are supplied.
5. Company and unit empty/failure/omitted states remain separate. A successful Company read must not hide a failed unit read. An authorized failed section shows a normal reload link to `/organization`, preserves successful content and never reports zero as a successful count. Omitted sections expose neither names nor existence markers.

### Payroll module (`src/payroll_workspace.rs`)

`pub(crate) fn body(runs: ScreenSection<RunSummary>) -> impl IntoView` replaces current payroll_body through root-owned hookup. Preserve `AuthorizedRuns` implementation/export and hydration contract exactly for this SSR lane. Wrap that working status-filter/list in the task layout; do not add a second selector, dead search, fake schedule control or change client code without a separately admitted rebuilt bundle.

1. Root supplies the single page-level h1 (focused route “급여”, Home “내 업무”); module uses section headings only. Description that these are visible run records, and a six-stage ordered guide (`aria-label="급여 처리 순서"`): 원천 확인 →계산 →예외 검토 →독립 검토 →명세서·지급 지시 →지급 대사. Label it guidance; never use aria-current/completed checks for multiple unrelated runs or infer completed stages from calculation_enabled.
2. The main “실행 기록” panel contains the existing working filter/list. It keeps exact period/source/status/timestamps and existing contract attributes. No per-run mirror, disclosure or separate status panel is added outside the filtered island: it could remain visible when the working filter hides that run. This lane changes only the surrounding SSR layout and non-run-specific guidance. A redesigned hydrated row, exact record inspector and unknown-status treatment require the genuine bundle redesign lane.
3. The right “검토 전 확인” card provides clear approval consequences: review the same period/source/revision, resolve source discrepancies, and retain the review record. The distinct “검토 자료” area is a non-run-specific checklist of the evidence to examine when opening the owning record; it repeats no record values, selection, counts or status outside the working filter. Do not populate exception counts, legal evidence, owner names, totals, reviewers or receipts from RunSummary; none exists in that projection. A listed source label is not proof that evidence was verified.
4. Persistent visible notice: “승인은 지급 완료를 의미하지 않습니다”. Instruction export/download also must never imply settlement. There is no direct-payment button or automatic-bank-transfer claim.
5. Status labels remain entirely within the unchanged AuthorizedRuns island in this lane. In the separately admitted native-bundle redesign, known raw statuses may get explanatory labels and unknown statuses must show “상태 확인 필요” with the exact raw value, never approved/paid fallback. The two current lifecycle vocabularies are not identical: legacy domain has STAGED/BLOCKED_LEGAL_GATE/READY_FOR_REVIEW/APPROVED/ISSUED/VOID; adapter also uses ATTENDANCE_CLOSED/CALCULATED/SUBMITTED/REJECTED/SCHEDULED/SUBMITTED_TO_BANK/PAID/FAILED. No frontend state machine performs business transitions.
6. Empty and failure keep existing truthful text; failure has a real reload link to `/payroll`. Omitted remains byte-equal unauthorized shell. No action buttons/forms are rendered from the summary alone because read access/calculation_enabled do not establish decision authority.

## Full task layout after owner projection wiring (required release work, not faked now)

The structural renderer above is not complete organization change or payroll approval acceptance. Module UI comes first per user; the following exact facts/commands must fill its working inspector when wiring lands:

| Area | Real available source | UI destination / required guard |
|---|---|---|
| Payroll subject, period, status | adapter PayrollRunDetail.run | Header; Company scope must additionally come from current authorized context, never guess from line labels |
| Submitter/reviewer/time/reason | adapter run submitted_by/submitted_at/decided_by/decided_at/decision_reason/approval_ref | Participant history and decision outcome; IDs resolved only through authorized labels |
| Exceptions | PayrollRunDetail exceptions_open/total plus lifecycle PayrollException page | Discrepancy list beside source/person refs; no completion if data missing or page truncated |
| Source and legal evidence | PayrollRunDetail source_summary/legal_basis | Typed allowlisted evidence projection with exact source refs, not arbitrary JSON dumped to product UI |
| Calculated result | RunCalcSummary version/calculated_at/calculated_lines/blocked_lines/payable/total_net_won | Exact reviewed revision and calculation counts; total only if present/authorized; payable=false never “지급 가능” |
| Readiness lines | PayrollLineSummary | Real attendance/source readiness; these contain no wage amounts, never dress them up as issued statements |
| Approval command | POST runs/{id}/decision via owner, APPROVE or REJECT; reject requires reason; owner checks distinct natural persons | Two actual actions with reason by decision; no third “return” command invented from prototype. UI must carry current revision/command identity once owning contract supports them |
| Rejection repair | legacy withdraw exists only from REJECTED and resets head decision fields | Do not call this append-only supersession. Durable revision/history contract is a wiring blocker; UI preserves evidence and exposes truthful recovery when implemented |
| Payment/statement progress | disbursement, payslip_delivery owner projections | Separate delivery, acknowledgement and reconciliation; issued != acknowledged, approved != paid |
| Organization change | canonical orgchange/application/domain workflow (requires separately authorized projection) | Current/proposed values, effective date, dependencies, reviewers, draft/save/submit/history, per-child outcome and recovery |

Approval inspector final layout: subject + scope + status/owner/period; exact reviewed revision; ordered required evidence/discrepancies; participants/history; consequences immediately above reason field and owner-authorized actions; durable result/receipt/reopen links. Wide: inspector beside work. Narrow: one continuous page with skip links, no content loss or sideways scrolling. Conflict/unknown outcomes preserve typed inputs and require receipt reconciliation, never a success toast or blind retry. Controls appear only when wired to real owning use cases; native no-JS form fallback and CSRF/current authorization are owner integration requirements.

## Test and admission packet

`workflow_presentation_tests.rs`: seven unit tests, invoked through current `render_screens` only; `tests.patch` contains the new test file and a cfg(test,ssr) module hookup. All fixtures are ordinary test inputs and never compiled into product renderer routes. No prior test edits/deletions. Root applies reviewed test patch, builds using the existing Buck unit target, verifies exact seven discovery names, then executes. A missing schema/tool, compile error or zero discovery is a prerequisite failure, not RED. Expected semantic failures are current absent hierarchy/context, swallowed partial section failure, non-run-specific review guidance and section-local recovery links.

Exact initial semantic RED command: `tools/buck2 run //backend/crates/payroll/ui:console-payroll-ui-unit -- --exact workflow_presentation_tests::organization_preserves_partial_read_failure_and_offers_real_reload`. Discover exactly one first using the same command with `--list --exact` before the leaf name. Full candidate invocation: `tools/buck2 run //backend/crates/payroll/ui:console-payroll-ui-unit -- workflow_presentation_tests::` after discovery confirms exactly7 leaves; complete preserved regression command: `tools/buck2 test //backend/crates/payroll/ui:console-payroll-ui-unit`. Do not assert19 total if other admitted tests have landed. No test/build was run by this author under the Company lease.

Root serializes test hookup, test baseline ratchet if required, sharedlib dispatch, theme files/resource mappings, generated BUCK, bundle manifests and authority records. Module ownership proposed only `organization.rs` and `payroll_workspace.rs`. The new source set still invalidates the existing bundle custody manifest even when SSR-only code compiles out; record truthful pending producer work and do not reseal artifacts. Static renderer acceptance and product release acceptance remain distinct.

Browser acceptance after implementation: actual product host/routes with UI-created real data and restricted permissions; screenshot the two page states and business inspector at1600/1280/320px plus200% zoom; keyboard/IME/focus and native details/reload/filter interaction; independent visual critique against the supplied screenshots; record adopt/adapt/reject against task outcomes. SSR fixture output alone is not browser or owner acceptance. No dedicated demo app/binary, seeded endpoint or fake login.

Pre-mortem: Company grouping invents a relation; hierarchy loops omit or duplicate units; partial failure becomes empty; status label invents settlement; summary grants an approval button; filtered rows disagree with sibling context; visual extraction changes island symbol; shared style regresses Company page. Detection: seven probes plus preserved13/regressions, exact browser interaction and independent review. Rollback: revert only admitted module dispatch/files/style changes in a new commit, preserving tests/evidence and Company work; do not rewrite history. Stop on source/bundle custody drift being bypassed, unsupported owner data, unresolved hierarchy security or competing file lease. Remaining HOLDs are full owner-projection/actions, authentic regenerated bundle, actual browser/restricted-policy/visual evidence and entire-release qualification.

Round2 response to root round1: eliminated per-run context duplication and moved unknown-status redesign to the native-bundle lane; added reverse sibling failure, failure-section-local retry, real UUID orphan/cycle inputs, duplicate-identity conflict and4096-node reversed-chain coverage. Proposal remains unexecuted pending independent review and compiler lease.
